# Without this, `docker build` sends the ENTIRE directory to the daemon before the Dockerfile's
# selective COPY lines ever run -- multi-GB _repo_archive/ and data/ trees included, even though
# nothing in them is ever copied into the image. Slow builds and, on a small /var/lib/docker
# partition, a build that fails on disk space for reasons that have nothing to do with the app.

.git/
_repo_archive/
data/
notebooks/
docs/
outputs/
tests/
_repo_archive/
*.ipynb
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
worklist.html
ningxia_local/

# Model weights NOT needed in the image build context beyond what Dockerfile explicitly COPYs
# (which is models/ as a whole, since it's small -- ~260MB tracked + the two Drive files that
# are gitignored and mounted at runtime, not baked in). Nothing extra to exclude here.
